findings.body:
**Build the successful-removal fixture paths from `REPO`, not the literal `/repo` path.**

The test uses a temporary `REPO`, but the literal `/repo/.git/cq-review-worktrees/...` target is outside the default review worktree root for that `REPO`. The `-C` expectation also names `/repo`, although the fixture's `repoRoot` is `REPO`. Derive the path from `REPO` in each removal case that uses the literal path. Keep the out-of-root refusal case (lines 124-139) on a path outside the root.

<details>
<summary>Suggested fix for the successful-removal case</summary>

```diff
   test('success removes the tree via git and prunes the registry entry', async () => {
     const calls: string[][] = [];
+    const target = join(REPO, '.git', 'cq-review-worktrees', 'pr-7-pr-7-fix');
     const registry = memRegistry({
       '7': {
-        path: '/repo/.git/cq-review-worktrees/pr-7-pr-7-fix',
+        path: target,
         branch: LABEL,
         createdAt: NOW - 1000,
       },
     });
     const model = mkModel([
-      { path: '/repo/.git/cq-review-worktrees/pr-7-pr-7-fix', branch: LABEL, head: SHA_B },
+      { path: target, branch: LABEL, head: SHA_B },
     ]);
     await removePrWorktree({
       ...baseOpts(model, registry, { run: fakeGit(model, calls) }),
-      path: '/repo/.git/cq-review-worktrees/pr-7-pr-7-fix',
+      path: target,
     });
     expect(calls[calls.length - 1]).toEqual([
       '-C',
-      '/repo',
+      REPO,
       'worktree',
       'remove',
-      '/repo/.git/cq-review-worktrees/pr-7-pr-7-fix',
+      target,
```

</details>

Apply the same substitution to the other removal fixtures that use the literal path, including the failed-removal, different-path, and lock tests. The `-C` expectation in each case must use `REPO` as well.
